-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/65fa2adb-aa2c-4d85-8555-dd92787b5137
-- title:
--   Integral of a grid lift is a Riemann sum
-- statement:
--   Let $D\subset\mathbb Z$ be finite, $h\ge0$ and $f:D\times D\to E$ with values in a Banach space. Then
--   $$
--   \int_{\mathbb R^2}\mathrm{gridLift}(D,h,f)(z)\,dz=\sum_{i,j\in D}h^2\,f(i,j).
--   $$
--
--   Each grid rectangle $[hi,h(i+1))\times[hj,h(j+1))$ has area $h^2$, so integrating the step function gives the Riemann sum of $f$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/TriangularHilbert/GridCell.lean#L101-L116

